<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Bids mixed.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Bids mixed.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-12-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dark northern spring wheat bids were mixed Tuesday across the northern U.S. grain belt, dealers said.</p>
<p>Dealers were split over the extent of cash wheat movement. One North Dakota dealer said Monday's drop in futures had scared off new movement. But a Montana dealer said he was still seeing a fair amount of mill business.</p>
<p>MGE spring wheat futures ended firm after gaining early on a light-volume rally, traders said.</p>
<p>March wheat on the MGE closed up 4-3/4 cents per bushel at $3.79, and May gained 2-1/4 to close at $3.62-3/4.</p>
